Here’s a focused review of the app with prioritized findings and concrete fixes. I’ve cited the specific files and symbols where applicable.

Critical

Logging leaks and verbosity in production
Files: POPin-Meet/routes.py, POPin-Meet/microsoft_calendar.py
Issue: We added many [DEBUG] prints (time slots, token, availability, Graph query params, event times). In production these can leak sensitive info (tokens, schedule patterns, potentially PII) and create noisy logs.
Fix:
Gate debug logs behind an environment config (e.g., APP_DEBUG_LOG_CAL=0/1). Wrap prints with if current_app.config.get('DEBUG_CAL', False).
Scrub identifiable values (token, emails) before logging.
Reduce to one summary line per request in production.
OAuth/session token handling in session
Files: POPin-Meet/routes.py (stores credentials in session dict), microsoft_calendar.py, google_calendar.py
Issue: Storing full credential blobs in server-side session (even if server-side) risks leakage and oversized cookies if misconfigured.
Fix:
Store tokens server-side in DB keyed by meeting token + a random session key; keep only a short opaque reference in session.
Encrypt at rest (e.g., Fernet) if DB used. Ensure refresh/expiry handled.
GET routes mutating state
Files: POPin-Meet/routes.py: /disconnect_calendar/, /disconnect_outlook/
Issue: State changes via GET make them CSRF-prone.
Fix:
Change to POST endpoints with CSRF protection (Flask-WTF) and form buttons.
Or at minimum add a signed token in the URL and verify.
High

Outlook date-time parsing edge cases fixed but needs guardrails
Files: POPin-Meet/microsoft_calendar.py: get_free_busy_info(), _parse_graph_dt
Issue: We now robustly parse Graph timestamps with 7-digit fractions and missing Z. Good, but this logic should be unit-tested to prevent regressions.
Fix:
Add tests for combinations: with/without Z, with 7-digit fractional seconds, TZ offsets.
Availability behavior coupling + UI assumptions
Files: POPin-Meet/templates/respond_meeting.html
Issue: Active provider logic prefers Google if both connected. This is a UX decision and should be explicit (banner does say which one is used now). However, a mismatch between banner and algorithm or stale availability dicts could confuse users.
Fix:
Offer a toggle control to pick which provider to use when both are connected, defaulting to Google.
Persist choice in session per token: session[f'av_source_{token}'] in routes.py.
Missing CSRF protection
Files: POPin-Meet/routes.py (forms), templates/*.html
Issue: Forms likely lack CSRF tokens.
Fix:
Add Flask-WTF, set SECRET_KEY and WTF_CSRF_ENABLED, include {{ form.csrf_token }} in forms.
Medium

Template hot reload expectation vs. production cache
Files: POPin-Meet/app.py or factory
Issue: Production likely runs without TEMPLATES_AUTO_RELOAD. We restarted service to pick template changes, but this should be a known requirement.
Fix:
Document: templates require restart in production.
For dev: app.config['TEMPLATES_AUTO_RELOAD'] = True guarded by FLASK_ENV=development.
Backup sprawl and mixed ownership on server
Paths: /home/ec2-user/apps/popin-meet/POPin-Meet/.bak
Issue: Multiple .bak, some owned by root, many variants. Can clutter and complicate.
Fix:
Rotate and prune backups (keep last N, e.g., 5).
Ensure operations run under ec2-user to avoid root-owned leftovers.
ICS filename sanitization
Files: POPin-Meet/routes.py -> download_ics()
Issue: Using meeting_title to form filename may include unsafe chars.
Fix:
Sanitize to safe ASCII, strip path separators, or use slugify.
Low

Error handling consistency
Files: microsoft_calendar.py, google_calendar.py
Issue: Some branches return {} (ambiguous), some return availability with indices False. Downstream expects dict of exact indices.
Fix:
Always return an index-aligned mapping. If query fails, default to False per slot to avoid empty map semantics.
Hard-coded defaults
Files: routes.py, microsoft_calendar.py, google_calendar.py
Issue: Default timezone 'US/Mountain' is repeated ad hoc.
Fix:
Centralize DEFAULT_TZ in a settings module.
GET endpoints lack rate limiting
Issue: OAuth callback and calendar checks could be spammed.
Fix:
Add simple rate limiting (Flask-Limiter) for calendar availability endpoints.
Security/Privacy hygiene

Secrets in repo or workspace
Paths: .env.server, “google and other credentials”, “twilio_2FA_recovery_code.txt”
Issue: Sensitive materials lying around.
Fix:
Ensure .gitignore covers them (it likely does), but review server filesystem too.
Use environment variables or secret manager for credentials.
Log redaction
Files: all calendar modules
Fix:
Redact tokens, authorization codes, refresh tokens from any DEBUG messages.
Reliability and Ops

Health check endpoint and readiness probe
Add /healthz (simple OK) and optionally /readiness to verify DB and critical integrations (optional).
Gunicorn settings
Ensure graceful timeouts and worker count appropriate for instance size; consider --graceful-timeout to allow external calls to finish.
Developer experience

Unit tests for availability
Add tests: Build slots_meta and mock Graph/Google responses, assert expected availability dicts.
Lint/format
Adopt ruff/black and apply across the project.
